2026-11-19T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2499) 'A portrait becomes a hair-card VRM inside the engine
 # uuid: 472b0d4d-ff14-5de7-af2c-8675cb813316
 # tags: rfd:title
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-19T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2499) 'one portrait becomes a VRM 1.0 avatar with hair cards and spring bones, in-engine.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2499) 'the hair-card guests, the viewer that runs them, and the masks they read.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2499) 'Can one portrait become a VRM with hair cards and spring bones inside the engine, with no Blender, no PyTorch and only openly licensed models?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2499) 'HairDeck (single image to hair cards, Apache-2.0) ships as Python on Blender. Its five models now run as ggml-rd (ggml on the engine's GPU) guests and match PyTorch within 5e-5. 26 portraits gave 26 VRMs in one viewer process, about 7 s each after a 20 s load. The masks still come from SAM 3 and BiRefNet in PyTorch. SAM 3 is under Meta's SAM licence.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2499) 'Run the viewer's batch mode on a folder of portraits, then open one VRM in a second reader. The check passes when every image gives a VRM and the window never stops for 4 s.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2499) 'Measurements behind the portrait-to-VRM pipeline
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2499) 'A portrait becomes a VRM 1.0 file in one engine process, with every model as a guest ELF or an engine module and no Python at run time.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2499) '- Text prompts become boxes through Bonsai 2 with its image projector, inside the engine (operator, 2026-11-19). SAM 2.1 base-plus turns each box into a mask, and BiRefNet-matting gives the person alpha, each as a guest ELF. SAM 3 leaves the pipeline.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2499) '- The VRM carries the hair cards, one spring chain per strand group, and a SOMA-X body with the ANNY identity (the reference rig) and its pose correctives, in a CC0 sport suit.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2499) '- The VRM's licence fields are CC0, and the repositories keep HairDeck's notices.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2499) '- All slow work runs on one worker thread. A stop over 4 s fails the run, and at 5 s the viewer ends itself.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2499) '- RFD66606-2478 (ANNY-soma-x keypoints), which held HairDeck's licence as unread.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2499) '- RFD66606-2311 (serving Bonsai 2), the same model served outside the engine.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2499) 'What was measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2499) 'Each guest was compared with HairDeck's PyTorch code in fp32 on the same inputs, as relative L2 error: the card VAE 1.3e-6, the image, chain and colour DiTs about 1e-6, DINOv3 1.4e-5, and the 50-step sampler 4.5e-5. The guests also run binary-translated, with results identical to the interpreted run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2499) 'Mask quality was measured against the SAM 3 masks on the same 26 images, given the box of the SAM 3 mask. SAM 2.1 base-plus reached a mean IoU of 0.83 on hair and 0.92 on face, and six hair masks fell below 0.7. SAM 2.1 large reached 0.85 and 0.91 at 2.6 times the encode time, so base-plus is the choice. Box detectors were measured on the same images by box IoU: OWLv2 base 0.87 on hair and 0.76 on face, Grounding DINO base 0.89 and 0.87.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2499) 'What was not measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2499) '- Bonsai 2's boxes. The engine's language module built its image projector code out, so the model never saw an image. The build fix is in review, and the 26-image box test waits on it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2499) '- SAM 2.1 and BiRefNet as guests. Both ran only natively or in PyTorch so far.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2499) '- The effect of the new masks on the cards, and whether a reader other than the VRM add-on used to write the file opens it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-19T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2499) '- The pose correctives when a bone turns. They are baked for the rest pose only.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2499  1 LINE
 Text:Written
